1. Overview

This data mapping document defines the field-level transformation and migration logic for moving active member data from the Enterprise Data Hub (EDH) to the target SQL schema for Microsoft Dataverse CRM. The mapping ensures strict data consistency, format standardization (E.164 for phone, RFC 5322 for email, ISO 8601 for dates, USPS for addresses), and type alignment between source and target systems. Key considerations include enforcing referential integrity, deduplication of Member IDs, and compliance with HIPAA and auditability requirements. Business rules and constraints such as mandatory fields, uniqueness, and data validation are actively applied to all mappings, shaping transformation logic and ensuring no data loss or orphaned records. All mappings are grounded in the provided DDLs, sample data, and explicit constraints, with no omissions or assumptions.

